Changes with respect to the original VAMP distribution:

- kinds: removed (superseded by kinds module in WHIZARD)

- tao_random_numbers: luxury functions removed (work around DEC compiler bug)

- divisions: 
    + added write_history (analogous to print_history)
    + rebinning_weights: smooth_d normalization put before non-zero check 

- vamp_rest:
    + extra integer argument for all sampling functions: process ID
    + added vamp_write_history (analogous to print_history)
    + vamp_sample_grid0: after loop_over_cells, do the rest only for g%mu(2)>0
    + vamp_average_iterations_grid: execute only if g%sum_weights>0,
             otherwise set numbers to zero
    + vamp_update_weights: execute only if sum(weights)>0,
             otherwise set weights to uniform value
    + vamp_sample_grids: 
        set integrals = std_devs = 0 before executing body 
	(??g%integrals/g%std_devs/g%active??)
        before calling vamp_refine_grid: active(ch) = (integrals(ch)/=0)
    + vamp_reduce_channels: execute only if any(active)
    + vamp_average_iterations_grids: execute only if (g%sum_weights>0),
	     otherwise set numbers to zero
    + vamp_next_event_multi: additional argument:
             real(kind=double), intent(out), optional :: excess
	     for wgt>1 don't do reweighting, but print weight and set
             excess = wgt-1 if present
    + vamp_warmup_grids: 
        before execution, recalculate weights skipping inactive channels 
        provide these as additional arguments to vamp_sample_grid0:
	     rng, g%grids(ch), func, ch, weights, g%grids, exc = exc     
    + read_grids_unit: use idum, not chdum in reading double/integer_array_fmt
    + vamp_print_histories: allow for three-digit channel indices
    + vamp_write_histories_unit: the same

- vamp_serial_mpi:
    + added vamp_write_history0

- vamp_parallel_mpi
    + added vamp_write_history (analogous to print_history)
    + vamp_sample_grids: 
	(??g%integrals/g%std_devs/g%active??)
        before calling vamp_refine_grid: 
	  set g%active(ch)=.false. if (g%integrals(ch)==0)
    + vamp_next_event_multi: additional argument:
             real(kind=double), intent(out), optional :: excess
	     for wgt>1 don't do reweighting, but print weight and set
             excess = wgt-1 if present

- constants: removed (superseded by constants in WHIZARD)

- histograms: 
    + added write_histogram1_unit
    + type histogram: added third column bins3 for collecting excess
	     weights and added corresponding functionality

- kinematics: removed

- phase_space: removed

